{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTranspose","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.GetD"],"declarations":39,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.kernel_summand_conj_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.kernel_summand_conj_mem","kind":"theorem","line":565,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L565-L570","doc":"Hypothesis-free summand pairing at enumeration members. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.kernelValue_conj_reindex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.kernelValue_conj_reindex","kind":"theorem","line":553,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L553-L563","doc":"**The `λ ↔ λ'` pairing of `kernelValue`, all `k`**: replacing every diagram by its conjugate\nin the kernel sum leaves `kernelValue k` unchanged. Combined with `kernel_summand_conj`\n(pointwise summand invariance) this is the full machine-checked statement of the conjugation\nsymmetry of the covariance kernel at every level — previously available only `decide`-bounded.\nScope-honest: a symmetry, not a sign — `covariance_kernel_conjecture` stays open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sum_map_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sum_map_conj","kind":"theorem","line":545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L545-L551","doc":"**Reindexing the kernel sum by conjugation** — for ANY integer summand `g`, summing\n`g ∘ conj` over `partsOf k` equals summing `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.map_conj_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.map_conj_perm","kind":"theorem","line":527,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L527-L543","doc":"**`conj` permutes `partsOf k`**: mapping the (nodup) enumeration through the involution\nreproduces it up to permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_mem_partsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_mem_partsOf","kind":"theorem","line":505,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L505-L525","doc":"**`conj` maps `partsOf k` into itself**: the conjugate of a partition of `k` is a partition\nof `k` (size preserved by `sum_conj`; sorted by `conj_sorted`; parts positive; parts `≤ k` since\na column height is at most the number of parts `≤ k`; length `= headD ≤ k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_pos","kind":"theorem","line":491,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L491-L503","doc":"Parts of `conj l` are positive: the count of parts exceeding `j < headD` includes the head. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.length_le_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.length_le_sum","kind":"theorem","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L481-L489","doc":"Positive lists have at least as many boxes as parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.partsFuel_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.partsFuel_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L469-L479","doc":"The enumeration has **no duplicates**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.nodup_flatMap_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.nodup_flatMap_cons","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L450-L467","doc":"Auxiliary: a `flatMap` of head-tagged families over a nodup index list is nodup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_partsFuel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_partsFuel","kind":"theorem","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L418-L448","doc":"**Completeness** of the enumeration: every weakly-decreasing positive list summing to `n`\nwith parts `≤ maxP` and at most `f` parts is a member of `partsFuel f n maxP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.partsOf_facts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.partsOf_facts","kind":"theorem","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L412-L416","doc":"The three `partsOf` member facts used downstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.partsFuel_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.partsFuel_mem","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L373-L410","doc":"**Soundness** of the enumeration: every member of `partsFuel f n maxP` is a weakly-decreasing\nlist of positive parts `≤ maxP` summing to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.kernel_summand_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.kernel_summand_conj","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L353-L364","doc":"**The covariance-kernel summand is invariant under genuine list-level conjugation, all `k`**:\n`(f^{λ'})³·ω₃(λ') = (f^λ)³·ω₃(λ)` for every sorted positive `l`. Both factors are separately\ninvariant (`sytDim_conj`, `omega3_conj`), so the kernel `Σ_λ (f^λ)³ ω₃(λ)` pairs off along\n`λ ↔ λ'` with self-conjugate diagrams as fixed points — at every level, not just `k ≤ 6`/`k ≤ 7`.\nScope-honest: a structural symmetry of the summand; it supplies **no** sign information\n(`YoungDiagramTranspose` proves the summand is transpose-even), so\n`covariance_kernel_conjecture` stays open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sytDim_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sytDim_conj","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L343-L349","doc":"**The hook-length dimension is conjugation-invariant** (list level):\n`sytDim (conj l) = sytDim l` — i.e. `f^{λ'} = f^λ`, since `|λ'| = |λ|` and the hook multiset is\npreserved. This is the remaining factor the kernel-summand pairing needed beyond `omega3_conj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.hookProd_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.hookProd_conj","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L330-L341","doc":"**Hook products are transpose-invariant** (list level): `hookProd (conj l) = hookProd l`.\nTransport the cell product along `cells_conj` and identify hooks pairwise via `conj_conj`\n(`hook_{λ'}(j,i) = hook_λ(i,j)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.hookProd_eq_prod_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.hookProd_eq_prod_cells","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L313-L328","doc":"`hookProd` as a product over the cell set (hook of `(i,j)` written in the definition's\nliteral `ℕ`-subtraction order). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.list_prod_map_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.list_prod_map_range","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L304-L311","doc":"List-range product = Finset-range product (ℕ; the `hookProd` inner/outer form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sum_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sum_conj","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L295-L300","doc":"**Conjugation preserves the size** `|λ'| = |λ|` — via the cell bijection, not arithmetic:\n`(conj l).sum = |cells (conj l)| = |transpose (cells l)| = |cells l| = l.sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.card_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.card_cells","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L284-L293","doc":"The cell count of a list diagram is its size: `|cells l| = Σ l_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sum_getD_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.sum_getD_range","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L274-L282","doc":"`Σ_{i < len} l_i = l.sum` in `getD` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_conj","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L258-L272","doc":"**`conj` is an involution on sorted positive lists**: `conj (conj l) = l`. The staircase\nequivalence makes this getD-extensional: `(conj (conj l))_c = min (headD) (l_c) = l_c`. Positivity\nis genuinely needed (a trailing `0` part is erased by `conj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.countP_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.countP_conj","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L246-L256","doc":"Counting parts of `conj l` exceeding `c` caps the staircase: `min (headD) (l_c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.countP_range_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.countP_range_lt","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L237-L244","doc":"Counting `j < k` over `List.range n` gives `min n k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L228-L235","doc":"`conj` of ANY list is weakly decreasing: the count of parts exceeding `j` is antitone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.length_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.length_conj","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L224-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.getD_zero_eq_headD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.getD_zero_eq_headD","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L221-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.omega3_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.omega3_conj","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L209-L217","doc":"**Conjugation-invariance of the 3-cycle class-sum eigenvalue `ω₃`, all `k`, all sorted `l`**\n(upgrading `omega3_conj_invariant_of_le_six`). Consequence: the covariance-kernel summand\n`(f^λ)³·ω₃(λ)` pairs off along `λ ↔ λ'` at every level `k` — provided the dimension is also\nconjugation-invariant, which holds by hook-length transpose symmetry and is the remaining\n(separate) list-level lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.contentSq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.contentSq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L201-L207","doc":"**Conjugation-invariance of the content square, all sorted `l`** — the general statement\n`YoungDiagramKernel` carried only as `decide`-bounded `k ≤ 6`\n(`contentSq_conj_invariant_of_le_six`). Transport through the cell model and apply the abstract\ntranspose-evenness `csq_transpose`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.cells_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.cells_conj","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L191-L199","doc":"**The bridge (sorry-free, all `k`).** On a weakly-decreasing list, the cell set of the\nlist-level conjugate is the coordinate-swap transpose of the cell set:\n`cells (conj l) = transpose (cells l)`. This is the statement the two parent files each assumed\nabout the other in prose. Proof: both memberships reduce to the staircase `r < l_c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L180-L189","doc":"Transpose membership is coordinate-swap membership. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.conj_getD","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L163-L176","doc":"**`conj` in `countP` normal form** on a sorted list: `(conj l)_c = #{x ∈ l : c < x}`, valid at\nevery index `c` (in range via the defining `range`-map, out of range because a sorted list has no\npart exceeding its head). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lt_countP_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lt_countP_iff","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L129-L161","doc":"**The staircase equivalence** for a weakly-decreasing list: `c < #{x ∈ l : r < x} ↔ r < l_c`.\nThe count of parts exceeding `r` is an initial segment of row indices, so membership of `c` in it\nis exactly the cell condition `r < l_c` — the heart of the transpose correspondence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_le_headD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_le_headD","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L119-L127","doc":"Every element of a weakly-decreasing list is at most its head. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.contentSq_eq_csq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.contentSq_eq_csq","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L102-L115","doc":"**`contentSq` is the cell-model `csq`.** The kernel file's row-nested list sum re-sums over\nthe cell set, so the abstract transpose-parity lemmas of `YoungDiagramTranspose` apply to the\nkernel's own content square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.contentSq_eq_finset_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.contentSq_eq_finset_sum","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L93-L100","doc":"`contentSq` as a nested `Finset.range` sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.inner_row_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.inner_row_sum","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L81-L91","doc":"The inner row sum in `contentSq`'s exact elaborated form (the `(j : ℤ)` binder ascription\ncoerces the `List.range` elementwise), re-expressed as a `Finset.range` sum. Stated with source\nsyntax identical to the definition so `rw` matches the unfolded term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.list_sum_map_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.list_sum_map_range","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L72-L79","doc":"List-range sum = Finset-range sum (the `List.range`-map form used by `contentSq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.mem_cells","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L56-L70","doc":"Cell membership is exactly `j < l_i` (the row bound `i < len` is implied: out-of-range rows\nare empty since `getD` defaults to `0`). No sortedness needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.cells","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.lean#L51-L54","doc":"The cell set `{(i, j) : i < len l, j < l_i}` of a list diagram, as a disjoint union of rows. ","signatureChunk":0}]}